{"complete":true,"city":"Kuwait City","template_id":"global-first-24-hours","title":"Your First 24 Hours in Kuwait City, Dealt as Cards","description":"A first-day sequence through Kuwait City’s religious, mercantile, textile, archival, architectural, and coastal layers—paced from an orienting morning to an open-air finish.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"entity_name":"Grand Mosque of Kuwait","title":"Grand Mosque of Kuwait","subtitle":"Arrival reset","notes":"Begin with the city’s largest mosque and a building designed with references to Kuwaiti and Gulf architecture. The Ministry of Awqaf offers an individual guided-tour request; arrange that directly before visiting.","short_summary":"Let a guided introduction to Islamic and local architectural language set the day’s scale.","source_url":"https://e.gov.kw/sites/kgoenglish/Pages/eServices/MOIAI/MOIAeservice.aspx","source_title":"e-Services – Ministry of Awqaf and Islamic Affairs | Kuwait Government Online","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Souq Al-Mubarakiya","title":"Souq Al-Mubarakiya","subtitle":"Breakfast and bearings","notes":"Use the souq as a working market, not a souvenir checklist. KUNA documents its food stalls, restaurants, spices, dates, clothing, perfumes, gold shops, and restored Mubarak Al-Kabeer kiosk.","short_summary":"Follow the alleys through the everyday overlap of food, trade, and old-city memory.","source_url":"https://www.kuna.net.kw/ArticleDetails.aspx?id=2775857&language=en","source_title":"Kuwait's Al-Mubarakiya Market: A Traditional Souk with Modern Appeal | KUNA","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"National Library of Kuwait","title":"National Library of Kuwait","subtitle":"The paper trail","notes":"Pause at the institution charged with documenting Kuwait’s intellectual output. Its official history traces the public-library lineage through the 1923 Al-Ahliyya Library and the 1994 decree establishing the national library.","short_summary":"Place the city’s modern cultural institutions inside a longer history of collecting and reading.","source_url":"https://www.nlk.gov.kw/Content.aspx?ID=23","source_title":"Historical Overview | National Library of Kuwait","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Kuwait National Museum","title":"Kuwait National Museum","subtitle":"The national frame","notes":"Make this the day’s formal museum stop. Kuwait’s National Council for Culture, Arts and Letters identifies it within its official museum network; consult the institution’s booking channel before setting out.","short_summary":"Shift from the market’s lived texture to the state museum’s deliberate frame.","source_url":"https://www.nccal.gov.kw/en/museums","source_title":"Museums | National Council for Culture, Arts and Letters","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Sadu House","title":"Sadu House","subtitle":"Material vocabulary","notes":"Look closely at how a domestic building became a home for textile practice. The society dates the house to 1936 and says it embraced weaving and textiles in 1980, continuing as a center for preserving that heritage.","short_summary":"Read Kuwait through woven structure, pattern, and the reuse of a seafront house.","source_url":"https://alsadu.org.kw/sadu-house-history/","source_title":"Sadu House History | Al Sadu Society","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"The Americani Cultural Centre – House of Islamic Antiquities","title":"The Americani Cultural Centre – House of Islamic Antiquities","subtitle":"Islamic-art lens","notes":"Use this stop to widen the visual field beyond Kuwait’s national story. NCCAL lists the center as the House of Islamic Antiquities within its museum network and provides an official visit-booking route.","short_summary":"Give Islamic material culture its own focused chapter in the afternoon.","source_url":"https://www.nccal.gov.kw/en/museums","source_title":"Museums | National Council for Culture, Arts and Letters","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Sheikh Jaber Al-Ahmad Cultural Centre","title":"Sheikh Jaber Al-Ahmad Cultural Centre","subtitle":"Architecture break","notes":"Walk the public complex with attention to its four jewel-like buildings. The center describes steel skeletons wrapped in titanium and glass, geometric forms informed by Islamic architecture, and extensive calligraphy across its pavilions.","short_summary":"Let contemporary cultural architecture answer the historic buildings encountered earlier.","source_url":"https://dev.jacc-kw.com/about-us/architecture/","source_title":"Architecture | Sheikh Jaber Al-Ahmad Cultural Centre","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Dickson House Cultural Centre","title":"Dickson House Cultural Centre","subtitle":"Diplomatic-era counterpoint","notes":"Enter Kuwait’s British political-agency history through a surviving house rather than an abstract timeline. KUNA reports that the building served as the agency until 1935 and was later restored as a cultural center.","short_summary":"Study a domestic building shaped by both Kuwaiti urban history and British diplomatic presence.","source_url":"https://www.kuna.net.kw/ArticleDetails.aspx?Language=en&id=2685113","source_title":"Dickson House Celebrates 17th Anniversary of Its Transformation into Cultural Centre | KUNA","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Kuwait Towers","title":"Kuwait Towers","subtitle":"Coastal orientation","notes":"Meet the skyline at its infrastructural roots. KUNA explains that the three-tower complex began as a water-storage project; the two taller towers hold water, while the smallest supports lighting and electricity.","short_summary":"Read the familiar silhouette as civic infrastructure translated into monumental form.","source_url":"https://www.kuna.net.kw/ArticlePrintPage.aspx?id=3276665&language=en","source_title":"Kuwait Towers: National Landmark, Icon of Contemporary Arab Heritage | KUNA","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Al Shaheed Park","title":"Al Shaheed Park","subtitle":"Evening decompression","notes":"Close outdoors, leaving room to process the day. The park’s documented landscape includes the Constitution Monument, lakes, gardens, an open theater, and museums addressing Kuwait’s battles and natural environment.","short_summary":"Finish among planted space, civic memory, and the modern city around it.","source_url":"https://www.kuna.net.kw/ArticleDetails.aspx?id=2427737&language=en","source_title":"His Highness the Amir Inaugurates Al-Shaheed Park Project | KUNA","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null}],"warnings":[]}
